.TH TOPO 1 "October 2026" "Topo review snapshot" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
topo \- destination-neutral infrastructure discovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B topo
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Topo collects infrastructure observations using locally approved, compiled-in
operations and publishes supported inventory to configured destinations.
The outbound ServiceNow worker requires separate administrator preparation,
restricted credential references, approved targets and independently verified
host identities. Installing Topo does not start discovery.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print the build version.
.TP
.B worker setup
Interactively configure the packaged Linux SSH worker, check registration,
and ask before enabling and starting the service. Requires root and a terminal.
.TP
.B worker check
Check the configured connection without collecting target inventory.
.TP
.B worker run
Run the outbound worker using explicitly supplied policy and credential references.
.TP
.B discover
Perform standalone discovery using the selected reviewed operation.
.TP
.B publish
Preview or explicitly apply supported destination publication.
.TP
.B serve
Run the separate standalone controller.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The packaged workers use independently prepared credential and policy files
under /etc/topo-worker or /etc/topo-agent. These directories are not populated
or overwritten by package installation or removal.
Use the installed documentation under /usr/share/doc/topo for complete commands,
identity, authorization, trust and supported-scope details.
.SH SECURITY
Never supply token or password values as command arguments. Use protected
credential references. Do not bypass SSH host-key or HTTPS certificate checks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR sysusers.d (5)
.PP
https://github.com/Nischoy-ai/topo
